  "details": "You already allow it via the camera. Just let us do it to our entire viewport but in a more constrained manner to prevent cheating in games, etc.\n\nI don't care if so many world creators rely on incredibly dark lighting to hide the fact that their textures are from an AI gen asset pack. I just want to be able to see wtf I'm looking at. Give me the gamma slider already.\n\nJust give world creators the option to enable/disable the adjustment of individual settings if needed so I don't need to find the prefab asset they may/may not of set up properly with 7 presets that range from 'cant see anything' to 'nuke your retinas' and no other options.",
